## Checks
1. Correctness. computeSessionExpiry (class-session.ts:46-67) gives now + 3 h, now + 7 d, and 17:00 Bangkok of the Bangkok date. It refuses 'until_17' at 17:00:00 and later. A missing field gives '3h'. It has no dependence on the server time zone. My TZ=America/Los_Angeles runs: domain 53 passed, app 32 passed.
2. F1. The refusal runs after authorizeClassroom (a read) and before ensureStudentCredentials. The writing fixture has a positive control (insert=2, update=2, audit=2). The refusal tests assert no insert, no update, no delete, no audit.
3. Callers. One production caller (handlers.ts:6-7). The z.input type keeps the { classroomId } callers compiling.
4. Error code. One Record (STATUS in http.ts) and it holds invalid_input: 400. Client code maps with if statements. No fall-through.
5. Panel. Default '3h'. The until_17 option hides from 17:00 Bangkok on. The body holds two keys. D-6 text in en and th is tested. Six keys exist in five locales. Option labels are visible with min-h-11.
6. Test meaning. Domain 96 passed and 12 skipped. App 82 passed. Nine student-login files: 168 total, 156 passed, 12 skipped. The real-db case was not rerun by me; the Green log records exit 0 with real_db_ran=1.
7. JSDoc. Present on every new or changed export. The comment of classSessionLifetime is wrong (F122).
8. Scope. No change in packages/db, card-token.ts, picture-password.ts, rate-limits.ts, codes.ts, credentials.ts, or another app. Added hash lines: 0.

## Findings (all nonblocking)
- F121: the state 'until_17' stays after the option hides at 17:00. Start posts it and the server refuses it. The teacher can recover.
- F122: wrong JSDoc text on classSessionLifetime (contracts.ts:37).
- F123: two statements on one line at class-session.ts:169.
- F124: the 7-day help text says 'until this time' with no time on screen. The double '3h' default is redundant.
- F125: no panel test posts 'until_17' and none covers the hidden-but-selected state.

## Not run
Domain aggregate suite, type checks, and the real-database run (heavy commands). I read their results from green-p1.log.

